  "records": {
    "description": "A double-buffered 16x16 color pixel screen. It takes horizontal and vertical coordinates and a hex number representing a colour, draws pixels into a buffer, can fill the whole buffer with a selected colour, and can draw the buffer to the display. Back buffer is pipelinable at 3 redstone ticks. The screen requires a texture pack that replaces redstone dots with coloured cubes.",
    "input": "Horizontal and vertical coordinates, plus a hex number representing colour.",
    "output": "Draws a pixel into a buffer; can fill the whole buffer with a selected colour and then draw the buffer to the display.",
    "speed": "Pipelinable at 3 redstone ticks.\n\nTo plot a single pixel: \n- Input Hex Color on the left levers\n- Input horizontal coord (middle levers) and vertical coord (right levers)\n- Press Draw Pixel in Buffer button\n- Press Draw Buffer button\n\nTo fill whole display with color:\n- Input Hex Color \n- Press Fill Buffer\n- Press Draw Buffer\n\nIt is double buffered so you can change any amount of pixels on internal buffer before plotting it to the screen. And obviously you need attached texture pack.",
    "considerations": [
      "Requires a texture pack that replaces redstone dots with coloured cubes.",
      "Uses specific texture packs: RGB Redstone 2.1 (attached) and a merged version of RGB Redstone 2.1 and Mattpack 1.21 (attached too) for development purposes."
    ],
    "notes": "Size: 16x16 pixels. Double-buffered. Authors: <@1081569090558246953> (base compact design) and <@158576177009786880> (syncing, harness and testing)."
  },
